menu "BTPDevice recovery"

    config BTPDEV_RECOVERY_TIMEOUT_MIN
        int "Minutes without an upload before going back to the application"
        default 10
        range 1 1440
        help
            Only when entered by `btp -recovery`. After a crash loop or a
            factory reset the recovery waits for a firmware (docs/PLANO.md D25).

    config BTPDEV_RECOVERY_AP
        bool "Own Wi-Fi network when no known network answers"
        default y
        select ESP_WIFI_SOFTAP_SUPPORT
        help
            With no network mirrored by the application, or after every known
            network failed once, the recovery also raises "btp-<name>" and
            serves its page at http://192.168.4.1/ (a phone opens it by
            itself: captive portal). Uploads stay authenticated by the key.
            Costs about 50 KB.

    config BTPDEV_RECOVERY_AP_PASSWORD
        string "Password of the own network (empty: open network)"
        default ""
        depends on BTPDEV_RECOVERY_AP
        help
            8 to 63 characters for WPA2. The upload is signed with the key
            either way; this only keeps strangers off the network.

    config BTPDEV_RECOVERY_INSECURE
        bool "DEVELOPMENT ONLY: accept uploads without the device key"
        default n
        help
            Without a key in NVS the recovery refuses every upload. This lets
            it accept them unauthenticated, for a bench before a key is
            provisioned. Anyone on the network can then flash the device.
endmenu
